agm: 1.0
package: api.security
version: 0.3.0
title: API Security Rules

node api.rules.input_validation
type: rules
summary: all API inputs must be validated against a schema before processing
priority: critical
stability: high
items:
  - validate_request_body_against_json_schema
  - reject_unexpected_fields_with_400
  - sanitize_string_fields_strip_control_characters
  - max_request_body_size_1mb
  - validate_path_parameters_pattern
  - validate_query_parameters_type_and_range
rationale:
  Unvalidated input is the leading vector for injection attacks and data
  corruption. Schema validation at the boundary prevents malformed data from
  propagating into the domain layer.
notes: Validation errors MUST return 400 with a structured error body listing all violations.
